      "title": "Cashfree Payments net loss at ₹118.5 cr in FY26; revenue jumps 51%",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/cashfree-payments-net-loss-at-118-5-cr-in-fy26-revenue-jumps-51-126082001251_1.html",
      "description": "Fintech firm Cashfree Payments India Private Limited has narrowed its consolidated net losses to Rs 118.5 crore in the financial year ended March  2026, according to the company's regulatory filings accessed via business intelligence platform Tofler.\nThe firm had posted a consolidated net loss of Rs 154 crore in the previous financial year (FY25).\nThe company's revenue from operations grew over 51 per cent to Rs 967.4 crore in FY26 from Rs 640.1 crore in the preceding fiscal.\nTotal revenue, which includes other income of Rs 5.04 crore, stood at Rs 972.5 crore for the period under review.\nOn the expenditure side, total expenses increased to Rs 1,090.9 crore in FY26, compared to Rs 794.7 crore in FY25.\nEmployee benefit expenses, however, saw a marginal decline to Rs 239.3 crore from Rs 243.4 crore in the year-ago period.\nAkash Sinha, Co-founder & CEO, Cashfree Payments, said: \"FY26 was one of the most consequential years for Cashfree Payments. We came close to the Rs 1,000 crore ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-20T17:57:08"
    },
